# Security

* Never hardcode secrets.
* Never expose private keys.
* Never commit credentials.
* Never log passwords.
* Never log access tokens.
* Never log payment credentials.
* Never weaken authentication.
* Never disable SSL/TLS verification.
* Never bypass certificate validation.
* Use secure storage for sensitive local data when the existing architecture supports it.
* Do not expose internal backend errors to users.
* Validate user input where appropriate.
* Preserve existing authorization behavior.

## Sensitive Data

Treat these as sensitive:

* Access tokens
* Refresh tokens
* Passwords
* Payment information
* Personal information
* Booking information
* Authentication data

Do not print or persist sensitive data unnecessarily.

